Gross Revenues include, by way of illustration and not
limitation, monthly and other fees charged Subscribers for Cable Services including Basic
Service, other Tiers of Cable Service, video on demand, pay-per-view and per-program channels,
Cable Service installation fees, Cable Service equipment rentals or sales and Franchise Fees.
Notwithstanding the foregoing, “Gross Revenues” shall not include:
(i) any taxes, fees or
assessments collected by Grantee from Subscribers for pass-through to a government agency,
including, without limitation, the FCC user fee, the Access Capital Grant, or any sales or utility
taxes, but Franchise Fees are included; (ii) unrecovered bad debt; (iii) deposits paid by
Subscribers; and (iv) any exclusions available under applicable law.
The parties acknowledge that Grantee may need to allocate Gross Revenues between Cable
Services (which are subject to the Franchise Fee) and non-Cable Services (which are not subject
to the Franchise Fee but may be subject to other fees an&or taxes), when these two types of
services are bundled together in a discounted package offered to Subscribers.
Grantee shall
make such allocation in accordance with GAAP, but in no event shall Grantee allocate Gross
Revenues between Cable Services and non-Cable Services where such services are bundled
together in a discounted package offered to Subscribers for the purpose of evading its Franchise
Fee obligations under this Franchise.
