This Franchise is a contract and neither party may take any unilateral action that materially
changes the mutual promises and covenants contained herein.
Pursuant to the foregoing, any
conflict between the provisions of this Franchise and the lawful exercise of the City’s Police
Powers shall be resolved in favor of the latter, but in any other conflict between Grantor’s
ordinances, resolutions, rules or regulations and the provisions of this Franchise, the provisions
of this Franchise shall govern.
2.3
Effective Date and Term of Franchise
(A)
This Franchise and the rights, privileges and authority granted hereunder shall
take effect on the date last signed by a party (the “Effective Date”), and shall terminate ten (10)
years later unless terminated sooner as hereinafter provided.
(B)
The grant of this Franchise shall have no effect on Grantee’s duty under the prior
franchise agreement or any ordinance in effect prior to the Effective Date to indemnify or insure
Grantor against acts and omissions occurring during the period that the prior franchise agreement
was in effect, nor shall it have any affect upon liability to pay all Franchise Fees, taxes, permit
fees and other payments to the City (for any prior years) that were due and owed under a prior
franchise agreement.
SECTION 3. FRANCifiSE FEE PAYMENT AND FINANCIAL CONTROLS
3.1
Franchise Fee
(A)
Amount of Fee.
Grantee shall pay to Grantor an annual Franchise Fee in an
amount equal to five percent (5%) of the annual Gross Revenues. The Franchise Fee may be
passed through to Subscribers as a line item on Subscriber bills or otherwise as Grantee chooses,
consistent with federal law.
Grantee shall not deduct from the Franchise Fee any items listed
under Section 622(g)(2) of the Cable Act (47 U.S.C. § 542(g)(2)). Grantee reserves its right to
offset from the Franchise Fee any payment made to Grantor if permitted by applicable law and
Grantor reserves its right to challenge the legality of any such offset.
(B)
Payment of Fee. Payment of the Franchise Fee due Grantor shall be made on a
quarterly basis, within forty-five (45) days of the close of each calendar quarter and transmitted
by electronic funds transfer to a bank account designated by Grantor. The payment period and
