3.6
Alternative Compensation
In the event the obligation of Grantee to compensate the City through Franchise Fees is
eliminated by State or federal law, and provided that such change in law contemplates that the
City may be lawfully compensated by a Cable Operator for use of the Rights-of-Way in some
other manner, and unless otherwise provided by State or federal law, then the Grantee shall
provide such alternative compensation to the City, provided that in any event such alternative
compensation does not exceed five percent (5%) of Grantee’s Gross Revenues.
SECTION 4. ADMIMSTRATION AND REGULATION
4.1
Authority
The City shall be vested with the power and right to reasonably regulate the exercise of
the privileges permitted by this Franchise in the public interest, or to delegate that power and
right, or any part thereof, to the extent permitted under federal, State and local law, to any agent
in its sole discretion.
4.2
Rate Regulation
Grantor shall have the right to exercise rate regulation to the extent authorized by law, or
to refrain from exercising such regulation for any period of time, at the sole discretion of
Grantor, if and when exercising rate regulation, Grantor shall abide by the terms and conditions
set forth by the FCC.
Nothing herein shall be construed to limit Grantee’s ability to offer or
provide bulk rate discounts or promotions.
4.3
Inspection of Records
Grantee shall permit any duly authorized representative of Grantor, upon receipt of
advance written notice, to examine during normal business hours and on a non-disruptive basis
any and all of Grantee’s records maintained by Grantee as is reasonably necessary to ensure
Grantee’s compliance with the material terms of this Franchise.
Such notice shall specifically
reference the subsection of the Franchise that is under review so that Grantee may organize the
necessary books and records for easy access by Grantor.
Grantee shall not be required to
maintain any books and records for Franchise compliance purposes longer than one (1) year
except for those pertaining to Franchise Fees, which shall be retained for three (3) years.
Grantee shall not be required to provide Subscriber information in violation of Section 631 of the
Cable Act.
Grantor agrees to treat as confidential any books, records or maps that constitute
proprietary or confidential information to the extent Grantee makes Grantor aware of such
confidentiality, if Grantor believes it must release any such confidential books, records, or maps
in the course of enforcing this Franchise, or for any other reason, it shall advise Grantee in
advance so that Grantee may take appropriate steps to protect its interests, if Grantee requests
that Grantor continue to oppose such release, then until otherwise ordered by a court or agency
of competent jurisdiction, Grantor agrees that, to the extent permitted by State and federal law, it
