The Access Channel shall be considered fully utilized if unduplicated
programming is delivered over it more than twenty-five (25) hours per week on average over a
four (4) month period.
Programming may be repeated on the Access Channel, but may be
counted toward the total average hours only with respect to the original showing plus one repeat
per day to be considered “unduplicated.”
As an example, a rebroadcast of a City Council
meeting twice per day shall be considered unduplicated for purposes of this subsection.
Character-generated programming may be included for purposes of this subsection, but may be
counted towards the total average hours only with respect to two (2) hours per day.
