7.3
Return Lines
(A)
For the period commencing on the Effective Date and ending on the earlier of (1)
the date the Return Line described in subsection 7.3(B) has been constructed and activated or (2)
March 31, 2020 (such earlier date, the “Transition Date”), Grantor shall deliver Access
programming to Grantee on a semimonthly basis via a mutually agreeable format for distribution
over the Access Channel on the Cable System, which Access programming shall be replayed by
Grantee on a continuous loop until new Access programming is delivered by Grantor for
distribution.
(B)
By the later of January 1, 2020, and six (6) months following the mutual
execution of a written agreement between Grantor and Grantee (or one or more of its affiliates)
with respect to transport and maintenance (the “Transport Agreement”), and conditioned upon
the mutual execution of the Transport Agreement, Grantee shall construct a Cable System return
line from 2101 O’NeiI Avenue, Cheyenne, WY 82001 (“City Hall”) to the Cable System
headend (the “Return Line”). Grantee shall select the materials and technology to be used for the
Return Line, provided that Grantee shall ensure that the materials and technology selected for the
Return Line shall enable the Access video programming to be sent from City Hall to the Cable
System headend in HID if uploaded to the Return Line in HID and that the Return Line is in
compliance with all applicable FCC regulations.
Other than the Return Line Capital Grant
described in subsection 7.5(C), all costs associated with the construction and maintenance of, and
transport of Access video programming over, the Return Line, including applicable equipment,
shall be the responsibility of Grantor.
(C)
In the event that Grantor determines during the term of this Agreement that the
Return Line described under subsection 7.3(B) needs to be upgraded in any manner (an
“Upgraded Return Line”), Grantor shall provide written notice of same to Grantee. Grantee shall
select the materials and technology to be used for the Upgraded Return Line, provided that
Grantee shall ensure that the materials and technology selected for the Upgraded Return Line
