SECTION 4. COMPLAINT PROCEDURE
4.1.
Complaints to the City.
(i)
Any Customer who is dissatisfied with any proposed response of Grantee or who
has not received a response within the thirty (30) day period as required with respect to an
unresolved complaint in Section 3.7.(ii) shall be entitled to have the complaint reviewed by the
City or its designee.
(ii)
The Customer may initiate the review by filing a written complaint together with
Grantee’s written response, if any, with the City.
(iii)
The Customer shall make such filing and notification within thirty (30) days of
receipt of Grantee’s response or, if no response has been provided, within forty-five (45) days
after filing the original complaint with Grantee.
The Customer shall notify Grantee that a
complaint has been filed with the City by mailing a copy of the complaint to Grantee by certified
mail, return receipt requested.
(iv)
Grantee shall file a written response to the complaint with the City within fifteen
(15) days of receipt of a copy of the complaint from the Customer.
(v)
If the City or its designee decides that further evidence is warranted, the City or
its designee may require Grantee and the Customer to submit, within ten (10) days of notice
thereof, a written statement of the facts and arguments in support of their respective positions.
32
Active/S0027934.3
```

### Page 33 of 36

```text
(vi)
Grantee and the Customer shall produce any additional evidence, including any
reports from Grantee, which the City or its designee may deem necessary to an understanding
and determination of the complaint.
(vii)
The City or its designee shall issue a determination within fifteen (15) days after
examining the materials submitted, setting forth its basis for the determination.
(viii)
The City or its designee may extend these time limits for reasonable cause and
may intercede and attempt to negotiate an informal resolution.
(ix)
if the City determines that the Customer’s written complaint is valid and that
Grantee did not provide the complaining Customer with the proper resolution, the City may
require Grantee to grant a specific solution in accordance with the Grantee’s policies or resolve
the matter as otherwise mutually agreed upon by the Grantee and the City. if the City finds that
the Customer’s written complaint has no validity, the complaint shall be dismissed with no
further action being taken.
4.2.
Overall Oualitv of Service.
The City may evaluate the overall quality of Customer
service provided by Grantee to Customers:
(i)
In conjunction with any performance review provided for in the Franchise with
the City; and
(ii)
At any other time, at its sole discretion based on the number of written Customer
complaints received by Grantee and the City, and Grantee’s response to those complaints.
4.3.
Non-Compliance with Customer Service Standards. Non-compliance with any provision
of these Standards is a violation of the Franchise.
SECTION 5. MISCELLANEOUS
5.1.
Severability.
Should any section, subsection, paragraph, sentence, clause, phrase, term,
or provision of these Standards be determined to be illegal, invalid, or unconstitutional by any
court or agency of competent jurisdiction, such determination shall have no effect on the validity
of any other section, subsection, paragraph, sentence, clause, phrase, term, or provision of these
Standards, each of which shall remain in full force and effect.
5.2.
Non-Waiver.
Failure of the City to enforce any provision of these Standards shall not
operate as a waiver of said provision, or any other provision of these Standards.
5.3
Identification. All employees of Grantee and its contractors or subcontractors who are in
personal contact with Subscribers shall have identification cards with their name and photograph.
